---
import CalculatorLayout from "@/layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro"

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How are walking calories estimated?",
    a: "The calculator uses MET values (Metabolic Equivalent of Task) for walking at different paces. Calories equal MET × your weight in kilograms × time in hours, a standard approach in exercise science.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does walking speed matter?",
    a: "Yes. Faster walking has a higher MET value, so you burn more calories per minute. Walking uphill or on rough terrain also increases energy use beyond what this flat-ground estimate assumes.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why is my fitness tracker different?",
    a: "Trackers use heart rate, stride, and other sensors, so their numbers can differ. All calorie figures — including this one — are estimates, so expect some variation between methods.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does body weight change the result?",
    a: "Yes. Heavier bodies use more energy to move, so calories burned rise with body weight for the same pace and duration.",
  },
]
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Walking Calories Calculator — Calories Burned Walking"
  description="Estimate calories burned on a walk from your weight, pace, and duration using MET values. Free walking calorie calculator in metric and imperial units."
  heading="Walking Calories Calculator"
  intro="Estimate how many calories you burn on a walk based on your weight, walking pace, and how long you walk."
  slug="walking-calories"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <div slot="tool" class="tool">
    <div class="unit-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Measurement system">
      <button type="button" data-unit="metric" aria-pressed="true">Metric</button>
      <button type="button" data-unit="imperial" aria-pressed="false">Imperial</button>
    </div>

    <form novalidate data-calc>
      <div data-metric>
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="weight-kg">Weight (kg)</label>
            <input id="weight-kg" name="weightKg" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="10" max="500" step="0.1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="weight-kg" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="speed-kmh">Pace (km/h)</label>
            <input id="speed-kmh" name="speedKmh" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="1" max="12" step="0.1" value="5" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="speed-kmh" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div data-imperial hidden>
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="weight-lb">Weight (lb)</label>
            <input id="weight-lb" name="weightLb" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="20" max="1100" step="0.1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="weight-lb" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="speed-mph">Pace (mph)</label>
            <input id="speed-mph" name="speedMph" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0.5" max="8" step="0.1" value="3" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="speed-mph" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="duration">Duration (minutes)</label>
        <input id="duration" name="duration" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="1" max="1440" step="1" value="30" />
        <span class="error" data-error-for="duration" role="alert"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="actions">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Calculate calories</button>
        <button type="reset" class="btn btn-ghost">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <div class="result" data-result hidden aria-live="polite">
      <p class="result-label">Estimated calories burned</p>
      <p class="result-value" data-value>—</p>
      <ul data-detail></ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="formula">
    <p>The calculator uses the MET (Metabolic Equivalent of Task) method:</p>
    <p class="formula">Calories = MET × weight (kg) × time (hours)</p>
    <p>Walking MET values rise with pace — from about 2.0 for a very slow stroll to roughly 6.3 for brisk power walking. Imperial inputs are converted to kilograms and km/h before the formula runs.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="example">
    <p><strong>Person:</strong> 70 kg, walking at 5 km/h (MET ≈ 4.3) for 30 minutes.</p>
    <p class="formula">Calories = 4.3 × 70 × 0.5 = 150.5 kcal</p>
    <p>They burn about <strong>150 calories</strong> and cover 2.5 km on that walk.</p>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>

<script>
  import { setupWalkingCalories } from "@/scripts/walking-calories"
  setupWalkingCalories()
</script>
